{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789968822,"nonce":"UayQOZc8R7xuypDab6zPLLvLYfg=","title":"Python: release facts of the hook-reading library functions are computed per run","message":"The library snapshot carries each function's release facts (returns_owned, returns_param) and the runtime seeds ModuleFacts from them, computing only the program's own functions. A fact is recorded only when it holds for every program: a library function whose facts read a hook's (an extern the library declares without a symbol, such as zb_hook_instance_str or zb_hook_unbox_instance, whose body the frontend generates per program) is left unrecorded, and so is any storage-returning caller of one, transitively. A function returning no storage is a firewall: both its facts are false whatever it calls, so zb_fatal and everything above it are recorded.\n\nFor the Lua library every hook is defined in the library, so all 1039 functions are recorded and the per-run facts build went from 13 ms to 0.2 ms on any Lua chunk. For the Python library 77 of 577 functions go unrecorded (ZYNTAX_TRACE_DROP=1 lists them at build time: zb_any_*, zb_call_N, zb_list_unbox_*, zb_dict_*, the repr family), and they are the large dynamic-dispatch bodies every program reaches, so the runtime still spends about 1.3 ms on them for a trivial program and 5 ms on a kernel that imports optparse (facts 2.1 to 1.6 ms on print(1); 14.5 to 7.9 ms on an empty util+optparse kernel, of which the rest is optparse's and the kernel's own functions).\n\nThe hooks' facts really are program dependent today: zb_hook_instance_str returns whatever the class's __str__ returns, owned or not, so the facts of the library function that returns the hook's result follow the program. To record those 77 as well the hooks need a contract the frontend keeps by construction (for example: every hook that returns storage returns storage the caller owns, copying a borrowed result), declared on the library's extern and checked at runtime against the generated body's facts (falling back to a full fixed point when it does not hold). ZYNTAX_CHECK_FACTS_SEED=1 recomputes the fixed point without seeds and panics on any disagreement, naming the function.","files":null}]}